{"article_ids": ["7271e53377de24d4"], "canonical_title": "PRQuant: Permutation Residual Quantization for Low-Overhead Inference", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.78, "description": "The paper presents PRQuant, a new quantization method that tackles the outlier‑driven accuracy loss in low‑bit linear layers. Unlike prior smoothing, rotation, or residual techniques, PRQuant aims to avoid weight bottlenecks and eliminates the heavy execution cost of online approaches by using a permutation‑based residual scheme.", "entities": [], "first_seen": "2026-09-22T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_7271e53377de24d4", "importance_score": 6.24, "last_updated": "2026-09-22T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-lg"]}
{"article_ids": ["1f462f4963220aae"], "canonical_title": "xAI’s Grok 4.6 is now available in Amazon Bedrock", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.96, "description": "xAI's Grok 4.6 model is now offered through Amazon Bedrock. The model supports a 500,000‑token context window, four distinct reasoning effort levels, and is accessible via both the bedrock-mantle and bedrock-runtime endpoints. It includes a Converse API and cross‑Region inference capability.", "entities": ["model:grok", "model:grok-4.6", "org:amazon", "org:xai"], "first_seen": "2026-09-21T18:30:34Z", "id": "evt_1f462f4963220aae", "importance_score": 5.64, "last_updated": "2026-09-21T18:30:34Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["7510ed85b0255a17"], "canonical_title": "Memory That Looks Forward: A Zero-Inference Prospective Term for Personal Memory Retrieval", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.8, "description": "Researchers propose a new retrieval mechanism for personal memory stores that operates prospectively and requires no inference at query time. Commitments are recorded in an explicit ledger as dated or trigger‑conditioned entries. When a ledger entry fires, linked memory items receive a multiplicative salience boost that is combined with standard embedding‑based retrieval scores.", "entities": [], "first_seen": "2026-09-22T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_7510ed85b0255a17", "importance_score": 5.49, "last_updated": "2026-09-22T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["4f34f6c24e9c2c73"], "canonical_title": "How Benchling secured multi-tenant AI agents with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "Benchling built a defense-in-depth security architecture to run untrusted, AI agent‑generated scientific code for thousands of life‑sciences tenants. The solution uses Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Code Interpreter in VPC mode together with Amazon Route 53 Resolver DNS Firewall and VPC endpoint policies to block data exfiltration, including via DNS.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "term:dns", "term:vpc"], "first_seen": "2026-09-21T16:27:34Z", "id": "evt_4f34f6c24e9c2c73", "importance_score": 5.49, "last_updated": "2026-09-21T16:27:34Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["790cf36b99eec5ab"], "canonical_title": "Muse, Meta's extraordinarily privileged AI assistant, has a serious 0-day", "category": "security", "confidence": 0.6, "description": "A serious 0-day vulnerability has been identified in Meta's Muse AI assistant. The flaw can be exploited with a simple ClickFix attack, enabling a full hijack of the agent's functionality.", "entities": ["org:meta"], "first_seen": "2026-09-21T22:24:38Z", "id": "evt_790cf36b99eec5ab", "importance_score": 5.467, "last_updated": "2026-09-21T22:24:38Z", "source_ids": ["ars-technica"]}
